F) Relationship Tensions

Mara and Daniel disagree on whether a memory belongs to its origin or its impact.

Mara and Lila maintain professional distance while hiding personal reliance dynamics.

Mara distrusts Arun’s reduction of emotion to metrics but needs his evidence.

Lila resents regulatory authority yet depends on it for access stability.

Daniel both needs and fears Mara’s professional judgment.

Arun views Mara as emotionally biased; she sees him as ethically detached.

G) Core Conflicts

External

Regulatory duty versus measurable public health impact

Economic survival tied to memory licensing

Classification of emotional dependency as medical necessity

Defining authenticity when collective emotional reinforcement exists

Internal (Mara)

Need for certainty versus tolerance of ambiguity

Desire to restore lost meaning versus acceptance of incompleteness

Professional detachment versus moral responsibility

Preservation of truth versus prevention of harm

H) Theme Statement

When emotional survival depends on shared experience, authenticity becomes a choice rather than a fact.

